  "worked_solution": "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\u222d}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/339d4658909da42d55a836af93c7fda425bbe8d0ce17f246b73a4ca28cb9f380.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9\\,\u27fa\\,z=\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070533/assets/879425adc3b1e78a7ea6a59740c9d8634ac13f62dea8eedc764bb5f1b07c92c2.png)\n\nHence, $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222d}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V & ={\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}2y[x]_{x=1}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{9-{y}^{2}}}4y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
